
Given a string s which consists of lowercase or uppercase letters, return the length of the longest palindrome that can be built with those letters.
Letters are case sensitive, for example, "Aa" is not considered a palindrome.

class Solution {
    public int longestPalindrome(String s) {
        // Frequency array for all ASCII characters (O(1) space)
        int[] charCounts = new int[128];
        
        // Count each character in one pass (O(n) time)
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            charCounts[c]++;
        }
        
        int length = 0;
        for (int count : charCounts) {
            // Add the pairs (e.g., if count is 5, 5 / 2 * 2 = 4)
            length += (count / 2) * 2;
        }
        
        // If our result is shorter than the original string, 
        // it means at least one character was left over for a center.
        if (length < s.length()) {
            length++;
        }
        
        return length;
    }
}
